ore_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.009947415359948376,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":22.2,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0009134505594884677,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.32711,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.789,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":78.9,"pf":[],"description_full":"EquipmentShare.com Inc. provides integrated, full-service construction solutions across equipment rental, sales, and technology. It offers rental of aerial work platforms, electric and hydraulic power tools, vehicles, trailers, attachments, agriculture and landscaping equipment, climate control, compaction, compressed air, concrete and masonry, earth moving, fluid solutions, forklifts and material handling, ground protection, industrial tooling, ladders and scaffolding, lighting and security, power solutions, surface preparation and cleaning products, storage solutions and containers; and welding, cutting, pipe fabrication, and other products., as well as safety, testing, and communication products. The company also provides equipment parts; event and site management; maintenance and repair; and other services. The company serves the construction industry in the United States through a network of dealers and online. EquipmentShare.com Inc. was formerly known as EquipmentShare Inc. The company was founded in 2014 and is based in Columbia, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jabbok  Schlacks | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $135,000 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $476K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $24K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $435 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["EquipmentShare.com Inc is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.7B market cap on $4.4B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 28%.","The business throws off $225M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.60\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 33% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 59% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5863086232980332},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $41.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-41548684.38},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 77/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 40% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (79% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Neil Chheda Acquires 13,390 EQPT Shares via October 26 Distribution","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/neil-chheda-acquires-13390-eqpt-shares-via-october-26-distribution","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793233729.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Investment Analysts\u2019 Recent Ratings Updates for EquipmentShare.com (EQPT)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/27/investment-analysts-recent-ratings-updates-for-equipmentshare-com-eqpt.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793127407.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.077,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"EquipmentShare.com (NASDAQ:EQPT) Stock Jumps 7.2% \u2013 Should You Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/27/e